# A step that writes a table and reads it back only to check it: the count decides whether `keep` panics and goes no
# further, so the table is where the route leaves its notes, in the codomain (mathematics.md, "A route's domain and
# codomain"; rule 4 of "The closed picture is the pushforward of the fine one"). The library's operations whose result
# the body names are steps: `let con = Connection::open(..)`, `let stored = con.query_row(..)`.

route ledger.main
step main/Ledger()
step main/Ledger.keep
step main/Ledger.keep/open
step main/Ledger.keep/query_row

line entry > main call
line main/Ledger() > Ledger·ledger@main/Ledger() value
line Ledger·ledger@main/Ledger() > main/Ledger.keep value
line main/Ledger.keep > Ledger·ledger@main/Ledger.keep value     # `&mut self`: keep changes the ledger
line main/Ledger.keep/open > _·con@main/Ledger.keep/open value
known #new line Ledger·ledger@main/Ledger() > main/Ledger.keep/open value  # K
line _·con@main/Ledger.keep/open > main/Ledger.keep/query_row value
known #101 line _·con@main/Ledger.keep/open > main/Ledger.keep value  # its own execute
line main/Ledger.keep/query_row > _·stored@main/Ledger.keep/query_row value
known #101 line _·stored@main/Ledger.keep/query_row > main/Ledger.keep value  # the check
line main/Ledger.keep > SQLite(notes) own

home Ledger·ledger@main/Ledger() main
home Ledger·ledger@main/Ledger.keep main
home _·con@main/Ledger.keep/open main/Ledger.keep
home _·stored@main/Ledger.keep/query_row main/Ledger.keep

side entry left
side SQLite(notes) right

# #101: a value made in the body and used by the body's own calls has no taker
# K: a value handed through a field reaches no step inside: `Connection::open(&self.path)` hands `self` (#121,
#    decision 1, cause 3: the reader's `held_in` skips `self` even inside an argument)
